Package: hybridForecast
Type: Package
Title: Hybrid Time Series Forecasting with Trend and Seasonality
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(person("Cao", "Nguyen", email = "cao.nguyen@health.wa.gov.au", role = c("aut", "cre")))
Description: Provides hybrid methods for time series forecasting that combine
    machine learning learners (e.g., 'xgboost', 'lightgbm', and neural networks via 'torch')
    with trend and seasonal decomposition, changepoint detection, and rolling-origin
    cross-validation. Includes Bayesian hyperparameter optimisation using
    'rBayesianOptimization', support for exogenous regressors, automated handling of
    missing values and outliers, and prediction interval estimation. Designed for
    robust forecasting of complex, noisy series in operational settings.
